{
  "name": "minimax-h3",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "task": "image-to-video",
  "tasks": [
    "image-to-video",
    "text-to-video"
  ],
  "advert": {
    "what": "A still of a person becomes a moving shot of that same person: MiniMax-H3 ref2va keeps the face from your reference image and invents the scene around it. Three and a half seconds of video with its own generated audio track.",
    "time": "measured on this node: ~705 s per sampling step over 30 steps, so 6-7 hours per 90-frame 720x480 clip including VAE decode and the audio mux. Plan a night, not an afternoon.",
    "karma": 4
  },
  "provider": {
    "name": "stable-diffusion.cpp",
    "repo": "https://github.com/leejet/stable-diffusion.cpp",
    "launch": "{{sdDir}}/sd-cli.exe --diffusion-model {{sdDir}}/models/diffusion_models/minimax_h3_ref2va_pruned-Q4_K_M.gguf --vae {{sdDir}}/models/vae/minimax_h3_video_vae_fp16.safetensors --audio-vae {{sdDir}}/models/vae/minimax_h3_audio_vae_fp32.safetensors --llm {{sdDir}}/models/text_encoders/qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3-Q4_K_M.gguf --backend llm=cpu,vae=vulkan0 --diffusion-fa --rng cpu -p \"{{prompt}}\" -n \"{{negative}}\" {{imageFlag}} \"{{image}}\" {{endArg}} --sampling-method {{sampler}} -W {{width}} -H {{height}} --video-frames {{frames}} --steps {{steps}} --cfg-scale {{cfg}} --fps {{fps}} --seed {{seed}} -o \"{{output}}\" -v",
    "probe": "sd-cli.exe --list-devices",
    "update": "unpack a newer win-vulkan-x64 zip as a new kit folder and repoint sdDir; never reorganise 813-bfbef5b\\models - this kit reaches it through a junction",
    "note": "imageFlag is -r for mode=identity (Ref2VA) and -i for mode=start-frame (FL2VA); endArg is --end-img \"path\" only when an end frame accompanies a start frame. Both are the runner job, not the form."
  },
  "models": [
    {
      "family": "MiniMax-H3 ref2va",
      "quant": "Q4_K_M",
      "file": "minimax_h3_ref2va_pruned-Q4_K_M.gguf",
      "sha256": "9ca1aef9f4609a56c2c751484013e1b20fe352f892122e5ab0a428fb95a7956e",
      "bytes": 11420663904,
      "role": "identity",
      "vramGb": 15,
      "inputs": {
        "variant": "ref2va"
      },
      "note": "the identity model: your reference photo keeps the face. Needs the 5.2 GB video VAE, the 0.6 GB audio VAE and the 17 GB Qwen3VL-32B text encoder, all on disk in the kit."
    },
    {
      "family": "MiniMax-H3 fl2va",
      "quant": "Q4_K",
      "file": "minimax_h3_fl2va_pruned-Q4_K.gguf",
      "sha256": "dd948e08ad0ba3c71bd42f368e283dd82e790f5122a63b276e22a3e0283d0c10",
      "bytes": 11420663904,
      "role": "text-to-video",
      "vramGb": 15,
      "inputs": {
        "variant": "fl2va"
      },
      "note": "the text-only variant: no reference image at all, the scene comes from words alone. Same size, same VAE, same text encoder."
    }
  ],
  "variables": {
    "init": [
      {
        "name": "sdDir",
        "label": "sd.cpp kit",
        "type": "text",
        "default": "C:/Users/User/Desktop/sd-master-c678dfe-bin-win-vulkan-x64",
        "help": "The video kit. Its models folder is a JUNCTION into sd-master-813-bfbef5b\\models - the one physical copy. Do not move or delete 813 models."
      },
      {
        "name": "outDir",
        "label": "Output folder",
        "type": "text",
        "default": "C:/Users/User/Desktop/make_video/output"
      }
    ],
    "input": [
      {
        "name": "mode",
        "label": "Mode — what your image is",
        "type": "select",
        "default": "start-frame",
        "options": [
          "start-frame",
          "identity"
        ],
        "help": "start-frame (FL2VA): your image becomes the video’s first frame. identity (Ref2VA): your image is the face, the scene around it is invented."
      },
      {
        "name": "image",
        "label": "Image (start frame, or identity reference)",
        "type": "text",
        "required": true,
        "full": true,
        "help": "Full path to a PNG/JPG. This is either the first frame or the face that survives — the mode above says which."
      },
      {
        "name": "end",
        "label": "End frame (optional)",
        "type": "text",
        "full": true,
        "help": "Steers the last frame (flf2v). Only meaningful when the mode is start-frame; empty means the model chooses the ending."
      },
      {
        "name": "prompt",
        "label": "Prompt",
        "type": "textarea",
        "required": true,
        "full": true,
        "help": "Describe the motion and the scene: \"she slowly turns her head and smiles, wind in her hair, cinematic\"."
      },
      {
        "name": "negative",
        "label": "Negative prompt",
        "type": "textarea",
        "full": true,
        "help": "What should be excluded. Empty by default."
      },
      {
        "name": "width",
        "label": "Width",
        "type": "number",
        "default": 720,
        "min": 256,
        "max": 864,
        "step": 8,
        "help": "720 is padded to 736 internally - normal, not a bug. 864x480 is the OOM-risk size on 16 GB."
      },
      {
        "name": "height",
        "label": "Height",
        "type": "number",
        "default": 480,
        "min": 256,
        "max": 576,
        "step": 8
      },
      {
        "name": "frames",
        "label": "Frames",
        "type": "number",
        "default": 90,
        "min": 30,
        "max": 121,
        "help": "90 frames at 24 fps = 3.75 s. More frames is more hours, roughly linear."
      },
      {
        "name": "steps",
        "label": "Steps",
        "type": "number",
        "default": 30,
        "min": 10,
        "max": 40,
        "help": "30 is the tuned number for this model. Do not raise it hoping for quality - it costs hours per step."
      },
      {
        "name": "cfg",
        "label": "CFG scale",
        "type": "number",
        "default": 1,
        "min": 1,
        "max": 4,
        "step": 0.1
      },
      {
        "name": "sampler",
        "label": "Sampler",
        "type": "select",
        "default": "euler",
        "options": [
          "euler",
          "euler_a",
          "heun",
          "dpm2",
          "dpm++2m"
        ],
        "help": "euler is what the tuned runs used."
      },
      {
        "name": "fps",
        "label": "FPS",
        "type": "number",
        "default": 24,
        "min": 12,
        "max": 30,
        "muted": true
      },
      {
        "name": "seed",
        "label": "Seed",
        "type": "number",
        "default": -1
      },
      {
        "name": "output",
        "label": "Save video as",
        "type": "text",
        "role": "output",
        "default": "C:/Users/User/Desktop/make_video/output/h3_clip.avi",
        "help": "AVI carries the generated audio track - do not convert it away."
      }
    ],
    "files": []
  },
  "modes": [
    {
      "name": "ref2va-720x480",
      "fits": {
        "vramGbMin": "16",
        "note": "the proven cell here: 720x480, 90 frames, 30 steps, llm on CPU"
      },
      "karma": 4,
      "models": [
        {
          "path": "C:/Users/User/Desktop/sd-master-813-bfbef5b-bin-win-vulkan-x64/models/diffusion_models/minimax_h3_ref2va_pruned-Q4_K_M.gguf",
          "note": "identity reference only - the image is never a frame"
        },
        {
          "path": "C:/Users/User/Desktop/sd-master-813-bfbef5b-bin-win-vulkan-x64/models/vae/minimax_h3_video_vae_fp16.safetensors"
        },
        {
          "path": "C:/Users/User/Desktop/sd-master-813-bfbef5b-bin-win-vulkan-x64/models/vae/minimax_h3_audio_vae_fp32.safetensors",
          "note": "the generated audio"
        },
        {
          "path": "C:/Users/User/Desktop/sd-master-813-bfbef5b-bin-win-vulkan-x64/models/text_encoders/qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3-Q4_K_M.gguf",
          "note": "17 GB conditioner - CPU resident, this is the RAM budget"
        }
      ],
      "install": {
        "steps": [
          "The kit folder is flat: sd-cli.exe at the top. models is a junction to the 813 kit - keep it that way.",
          "Confirm the junction: Get-Item <kit>\\models -Force | Select LinkType,Target",
          "Probe: sd-cli.exe --list-devices names the RX 6800 as Vulkan0."
        ],
        "note": "First-frame mode (fl2va) is a different checkpoint in the same folder; it is not this service yet."
      }
    }
  ],
  "needs": {
    "gpu": true,
    "vramGb": 15,
    "ramMb": 28000,
    "cores": 6,
    "diskGb": 25
  },
  "output": {
    "kind": "file",
    "location": "C:/Users/User/Desktop/make_video/output - one .avi per run",
    "description": "a 3.75 s AVI at 24 fps with an audio stream; frame 0 is NOT the reference image in ref2va mode"
  },
  "update": {
    "command": "new kit folder + repoint sdDir; models stay in the 813 junction",
    "note": "WHEN is the operator call."
  },
  "pages": {
    "ad": "<style>\n  html, body { margin: 0; background: #0d1117; }\n  .sv { font: 14px/1.65 system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, sans-serif; color: #d8dee9; background: #0d1117; padding: 18px 24px 30px; max-width: none; }\n  .sv h1 { font-size: 21px; font-weight: 600; margin: 16px 0 2px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }\n  .sv h2 { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: #8fb3d9; margin: 22px 0 6px; }\n  .sv p { margin: 6px 0; } .sv .dim { color: #7d8998; }\n  .sv ul { margin: 6px 0 6px 18px; padding: 0; } .sv li { margin: 3px 0; }\n  .sv .num { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: #e6edf3; }\n  .sv .k { border: 1px solid #2a323d; border-radius: 3px; padding: 0 6px; font-size: 12px; color: #c9d3df; }\n  .sv .rule { height: 1px; background: #1c232c; margin: 18px 0; }\n  .sv p, .sv ul { max-width: 720px; }\n  .sv .warn { border-left: 2px solid #6b4f3a; padding: 4px 0 4px 12px; margin: 10px 0; color: #cbb7a4; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"sv\">\n        <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 260\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A wide 1970s television with rabbit ears, and a stick man in a top hat walking inside it\">\n    <defs>\n      <radialGradient id=\"tvvign\" cx=\"50%\" cy=\"46%\" r=\"70%\">\n        <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#0d1117\" stop-opacity=\"0\"/>\n        <stop offset=\"62%\" stop-color=\"#0d1117\" stop-opacity=\"0\"/>\n        <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#0d1117\" stop-opacity=\".95\"/>\n      </radialGradient>\n      <radialGradient id=\"tvglow\" cx=\"50%\" cy=\"50%\" r=\"50%\">\n        <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#8fb3d9\" stop-opacity=\".16\"/>\n        <stop offset=\"70%\" stop-color=\"#8fb3d9\" stop-opacity=\".04\"/>\n        <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#8fb3d9\" stop-opacity=\"0\"/>\n      </radialGradient>\n      <clipPath id=\"tvclip\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"900\" height=\"260\"/></clipPath>\n    </defs>\n    <style>\n\n      /* fill-box: the pivot is a point on the limb itself, so a scale or translate on an\n         ancestor cannot fling the arm across the screen */\n      .tv-fig, .tv-legA, .tv-legB, .tv-armB, .tv-armTip, .tv-hat, .tv-headg, .tv-earL, .tv-earR {\n        transform-box: fill-box;\n      }\n      .tv-fig    { animation: tvBob 1.1s ease-in-out infinite; }\n      .tv-legA   { transform-origin: 100% 0%; animation: tvLegA 1.1s cubic-bezier(.45,0,.55,1) infinite; }\n      .tv-legB   { transform-origin: 0% 0%;   animation: tvLegB 1.1s cubic-bezier(.45,0,.55,1) infinite; }\n      .tv-armB   { transform-origin: 100% 0%; animation: tvArmB 1.1s cubic-bezier(.45,0,.55,1) infinite; }\n      .tv-armL   { transform-origin: 0% 0%;   animation: tvArmB 1.1s cubic-bezier(.45,0,.55,1) infinite reverse; }\n      /* two arms swap places: the walk arms fade out, the tipping arm fades in already bent */\n      .tv-armsWalk { animation: tvArmsHide 11s ease-in-out infinite; }\n      .tv-armTip   { opacity: 0; animation: tvTipShow 11s ease-in-out infinite; }\n      .tv-hat    { transform-origin: 50% 100%; animation: tvHat 11s ease-in-out infinite; }\n      .tv-headg  { transform-origin: 50% 100%; animation: tvHead 11s ease-in-out infinite; }\n      .tv-earL   { transform-origin: 100% 100%; animation: tvEarA 7s ease-in-out infinite; }\n      .tv-earR   { transform-origin: 0% 100%;   animation: tvEarB 7s ease-in-out infinite; }\n\n      @keyframes tvBob   { 0%,100% { transform: translateY(0); } 50% { transform: translateY(-2.2px); } }\n      @keyframes tvLegA  { 0%,100% { transform: rotate(15deg); } 50% { transform: rotate(-15deg); } }\n      @keyframes tvLegB  { 0%,100% { transform: rotate(-15deg); } 50% { transform: rotate(15deg); } }\n      @keyframes tvArmB  { 0%,100% { transform: rotate(-13deg); } 50% { transform: rotate(13deg); } }\n      @keyframes tvArmsHide { 0%,40% { opacity: 1; } 46%,60% { opacity: 0; } 66%,100% { opacity: 1; } }\n      @keyframes tvTipShow  { 0%,40% { opacity: 0; } 46%,60% { opacity: 1; } 66%,100% { opacity: 0; } }\n      @keyframes tvHat   { 0%,44% { transform: translate(0,0) rotate(0); } 50%,56% { transform: translate(0,-8px) rotate(-11deg); } 62%,100% { transform: translate(0,0) rotate(0); } }\n      @keyframes tvHead  { 0%,44% { transform: rotate(0); } 50%,58% { transform: rotate(-5deg); } 66%,100% { transform: rotate(0); } }\n      @keyframes tvEarA  { 0%,100% { transform: rotate(0); } 50% { transform: rotate(2.4deg); } }\n      @keyframes tvEarB  { 0%,100% { transform: rotate(0); } 50% { transform: rotate(-2.4deg); } }\n\n    </style>\n    <g clip-path=\"url(#tvclip)\">\n      <rect width=\"900\" height=\"260\" fill=\"#0d1117\"/>\n    <clipPath id=\"tv-screen\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"300\" height=\"120\"/></clipPath>\n      <ellipse cx=\"450\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"270\" ry=\"130\" fill=\"url(#tvglow)\"/>\n\n      <g transform=\"translate(450,150) scale(1.14) translate(-450,-150)\">\n        <!-- rabbit ears -->\n        <g stroke=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\">\n          <path class=\"tv-earL\" d=\"M442,64 L398,22\"/>\n          <path class=\"tv-earR\" d=\"M458,64 L502,26\"/>\n          <circle cx=\"398\" cy=\"22\" r=\"4.4\" fill=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke=\"none\"/>\n          <circle cx=\"502\" cy=\"26\" r=\"4.4\" fill=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke=\"none\"/>\n        </g>\n        <path d=\"M430,68 h40\" stroke=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n\n        <!-- the box -->\n        <rect x=\"244\" y=\"64\" width=\"412\" height=\"144\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#141c26\" stroke=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke-width=\"2.8\"/>\n        <rect x=\"258\" y=\"76\" width=\"300\" height=\"120\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#070c11\" stroke=\"#8fb3d9\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n\n        <!-- the dials and the speaker grille -->\n        <circle cx=\"596\" cy=\"104\" r=\"21\" fill=\"#101821\" stroke=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/>\n        <path d=\"M596,104 L608,93\" stroke=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n        <circle cx=\"596\" cy=\"160\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#101821\" stroke=\"#8fb3d9\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/>\n        <path d=\"M596,160 L604,152\" stroke=\"#8fb3d9\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n        <g stroke=\"#8fb3d9\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" opacity=\".5\">\n          <path d=\"M582,80 h28 M582,88 h28\"/>\n          <path d=\"M576,182 h40 M576,190 h40\"/>\n        </g>\n        <!-- channel plate, the one piece of print on the front -->\n        <rect x=\"574\" y=\"132\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#0a1016\" stroke=\"#8fb3d9\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" opacity=\".9\"/>\n        <g stroke=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" opacity=\".55\">\n          <path d=\"M582,136 v6 M590,136 v6 M598,136 v6 M606,136 v6 M614,136 v6\"/>\n        </g>\n\n        <!-- legs -->\n        <g stroke=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke-width=\"2.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\">\n          <path d=\"M330,208 L318,242\"/>\n          <path d=\"M570,208 L582,242\"/>\n          <path d=\"M318,242 h-16\"/>\n          <path d=\"M582,242 h16\"/>\n        </g>\n      </g>\n      <g transform=\"translate(258,76)\">\n        <g clip-path=\"url(#tv-screen)\">\n          <g transform=\"translate(4,-30) scale(1.2)\">\n          \n        <g class=\"tv-fig\">\n          <path class=\"tv-legA\" d=\"M142,96 L132,118\" stroke=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"/>\n          <path class=\"tv-legB\" d=\"M142,96 L152,118\" stroke=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"/>\n          <path d=\"M142,74 L142,96\" stroke=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n          <g class=\"tv-armsWalk\">\n            <path class=\"tv-armL\" d=\"M142,74 L126,90\" stroke=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"/>\n            <path class=\"tv-armB\" d=\"M142,74 L158,90\" stroke=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"/>\n          </g>\n          <!-- the tipping arm is drawn already bent, so the hand meets the brim -->\n          <path class=\"tv-armTip\" d=\"M142,74 C152,66 155,54 149,45\" stroke=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"/>\n          <g class=\"tv-headg\">\n            <circle cx=\"142\" cy=\"58\" r=\"13.5\" fill=\"#070c11\" stroke=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke-width=\"2.8\"/>\n            <circle cx=\"137\" cy=\"56\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#cfe3ff\"/>\n            <circle cx=\"147\" cy=\"56\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#cfe3ff\"/>\n            <path d=\"M137,62 q5,4 10,0\" stroke=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke-width=\"1.7\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n            <g class=\"tv-hat\">\n              <rect x=\"130\" y=\"32\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#101821\" stroke=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/>\n              <rect x=\"123\" y=\"45\" width=\"38\" height=\"4.2\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#101821\" stroke=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n              <path d=\"M130,41 h24\" stroke=\"#8fb3d9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" opacity=\".7\"/>\n            </g>\n          </g>\n        </g>\n          </g>\n        </g>\n        <g stroke=\"#8fb3d9\" stroke-width=\".55\" opacity=\".10\">\n          <path d=\"M0,7 h300\"/><path d=\"M0,14 h300\"/><path d=\"M0,21 h300\"/><path d=\"M0,28 h300\"/><path d=\"M0,35 h300\"/><path d=\"M0,42 h300\"/><path d=\"M0,49 h300\"/><path d=\"M0,56 h300\"/><path d=\"M0,63 h300\"/><path d=\"M0,70 h300\"/><path d=\"M0,77 h300\"/><path d=\"M0,84 h300\"/><path d=\"M0,91 h300\"/><path d=\"M0,98 h300\"/><path d=\"M0,105 h300\"/><path d=\"M0,112 h300\"/><path d=\"M0,119 h300\"/>\n        </g>\n        <rect width=\"300\" height=\"120\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1d2833\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n      </g>    <rect width=\"900\" height=\"260\" fill=\"url(#tvvign)\"/>\n    </g>\n  </svg>\n<h1>MiniMax-H3 &mdash; a still that moves</h1>\n<p class=\"dim\">stable-diffusion.cpp · ref2va · 720&times;480 · 90 frames · this node</p>\n<p>Give it one photograph and a sentence about the motion. The face stays; the world around it is generated, including the sound. <b>Karma</b> <span class=\"k\">4</span></p>\n\n<h2>What it makes</h2>\n<p>A <b>3.75 second</b> AVI at 24 fps with its own audio track. Identity-conditioned video &mdash; it is the same person, in a scene nobody shot.</p>\n\n<h2>What it needs here</h2>\n<ul><li>The RX 6800, and it wants nearly all of it.</li>\n<li><b>28 GB of RAM</b>: the 17 GB text encoder lives on the CPU for the whole run. This machine has 32 GB, so a browser tab is real competition.</li>\n<li>Nothing else on the GPU &mdash; no miner, no llama-server, no image server. One card, one job by habit, not by law.</li></ul>\n\n<h2>What it costs</h2>\n<p><span class=\"num\">~705 s per step</span>, 30 steps, then decode and mux: <b>6 to 7 hours</b> for one clip, measured on this node. Frame count scales roughly linearly, so 121 frames is not a small bump.</p>\n\n<h2>Where the output lands</h2>\n<p><code>Desktop\\make_video\\output\\h3_&lt;W&gt;x&lt;H&gt;_&lt;frames&gt;f_ref_&lt;timestamp&gt;.avi</code></p>\n\n<div class=\"rule\"></div>\n<h2>How to start it</h2>\n<p><b>Prepare this serve</b>, paste the reference image path, describe the motion, press run. Then leave it alone.</p>\n<div class=\"warn\"><b>ref2va is identity only.</b> Your photo is never frame 1. If the scene must BE the photo, that is the other checkpoint (fl2va) and it is not this service yet.</div>\n</div>",
    "inputs": "    <style>\n      html, body { margin: 0; background: #0d1117; }\n      .sv { font: 14px/1.6 system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, sans-serif; color: #d8dee9; background: #0d1117; padding: 20px 24px 30px; }\n      .sv h2 { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .1em; color: #5ad2a0; margin: 22px 0 6px; }\n      .sv h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }\n      .sv p { margin: 6px 0; max-width: 760px; }\n      .sv .dim { color: #7d8998; }\n      .sv pre { background: #0e1016; border-radius: 8px; padding: 11px; overflow: auto; font: 11.5px/1.55 ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace; color: #9fb0c9; margin: 8px 0; }\n      .sv code { font: 11.5px ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace; color: #c9d3df; }\n      .sv .box { border-left: 2px solid #2a323d; background: rgba(255,255,255,.02); padding: 9px 12px; margin: 10px 0; max-width: 760px; }\n      .sv .warn { color: #ffd479; }\n    </style>\n    <div class=\"sv\">\n    <h2>What a run does</h2>\n    <p>A load line (~30 s), then a step bar per sampling step. The log can sit stale for minutes &mdash; the bar-to-bar gap is the honest signal, not the file timestamp. At the end: <code>generate_video completed</code>, the VAE decode, then the mux.</p>\n    <p class=\"dim\">The same knobs as the video WebUI on 1235: start frame or identity, end frame, motion prompt, size, frames, steps, sampler.</p>\n\n    <h2>Before you press run</h2>\n    <div class=\"box\">Close the browser, stop unMiner, stop any <code>llama-server</code> and any <code>sd-server</code>. The engine decides where the weights live from <b>free RAM at load time</b>; a single open browser can flip it into a segmented, 100x slower plan that dies hours later.</div>\n\n    <h2>Where it lands</h2>\n    <p><code>Desktop&#92;make_video&#92;output&#92;</code> &mdash; keep the AVI as it is; it carries the generated audio track.</p>\n    </div>"
